From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Antonio Maiorano <amaiorano@google.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 06:07:50 -0700
Subject: Enable SplitBufferTextureCopyForOversizedRow on ARM, ImgTec, and
 Qualcomm

Several GPUs and drivers overflow or wrap around when copying between a
buffer and a texture with a large row pitch (>= 256 MiB / 0x10000000):
- ARM Mali GLES drivers overflow a signed 32-bit bit-stride calculation
  ((int32_t)(GL_PACK_ROW_LENGTH * bpp) * 8) and write subsequent rows at
  negative offsets before the PBO (crbug.com/569161611).
- ImgTec PowerVR GPUs/drivers fail with GL_INVALID_OPERATION on GLES or
  fail to write subsequent rows on Vulkan when the row byte stride
  reaches 2^28 (crbug.com/529867799).
- Qualcomm Adreno GPUs wrap row offsets at 256 MiB (2^28) back to 0 in
  buffer-texture copies (crbug.com/380487895).

Enable Toggle::SplitBufferTextureCopyForOversizedRow on ARM, ImgTec,
Intel, and Qualcomm in the OpenGL backend, on ImgTec and Qualcomm in the
Vulkan backend, and on Qualcomm in the D3D11 and D3D12 backends, so
copies with oversized rows are split into one copy command per row.

Bug: 569161611, 529867799, 380487895
Change-Id: I37b99e14ee9e17d6f1c4a0d693f75e12fe99050a
Reviewed-on: https://dawn-review.googlesource.com/c/dawn/+/351555
Reviewed-by: Corentin Wallez <cwallez@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Antonio Maiorano <amaiorano@google.com>

diff --git a/src/dawn/native/BufferTextureCopyOversizedRow.cpp b/src/dawn/native/BufferTextureCopyOversizedRow.cpp
index 09fb755f40f2c3dee91c820e834ffd2a468aedde..9d75fe128d2b7ce1c865d15d87ba3b3e97c54857 100644
--- a/src/dawn/native/BufferTextureCopyOversizedRow.cpp
+++ b/src/dawn/native/BufferTextureCopyOversizedRow.cpp
@@ -45,7 +45,10 @@ namespace {
 // hardware register fields: bytes per row is 18 bits and texels per row is 14 bits. The two must
 // be checked independently: bytesPerRow == texelsPerRow * bytesPerBlock, so a format with a small
 // bytesPerBlock (e.g. R8Unorm, 1 byte/texel) can push texelsPerRow past 2^14 while bytesPerRow is
-// still nowhere near 2^18. See https://crbug.com/481934465.
+// still nowhere near 2^18. See crbug.com/481934465.
+// These thresholds also cover the larger 256 MiB (2^28 bytes) row pitch overflow / wrap-around
+// limits on ARM Mali (crbug.com/569161611), ImgTec PowerVR (crbug.com/529867799),
+// and Qualcomm Adreno (crbug.com/380487895).
 constexpr uint64_t kMaxBytesPerRow = 1u << 18;
 constexpr uint64_t kMaxTexelsPerRow = 1u << 14;
 
